Z||000024||84Bill||12-04-2001||10:22 AM||||Someone ransacked my car lastnight! <P>I dont normaly lock it up since there is nothing worth having a broken window over in it. The guy was very brazen since he must have sat in it for a while and smoked a newport cigarette and put it out in my ashtray. All that was missing were my sunglasses and all the change and small bills in the side pocket. The face plate was removed from my cheap shitz roadgear cd stereo but everything was stil there and working.<P>I'll consider myself lucky. ||||reg||8
Z||000025||Tigger||12-04-2001||10:24 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by kneebarx:<BR><B>One word:<P>The Club!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Club isn't really a sure thing.  Still can hacksaw through the steering wheel in 15 seconds.<P>I saw a similar "Club" that locks around the brake pedal arm and extends to the floorboard so the pedal cannot be depressed which means the car isn't going anywhere, also could work on the clutch pedal.  It looked really convincing and was made of hardened steel so imagine trying to hacksaw through something like that with it up in the footwell.  Unfortunately, I can't remember the name of the product.<P>That sucks 84Bill  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 12-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000026||kneebarx||12-04-2001||11:10 AM||||Yea, I heard about that, you can saw off the wheel to get the club off.  Now they have ones that have the entire half of the wheel covered so you can't saw it off.  I would think that kind of "club" and an alarm would deter most petty thieves.  And of course, if it's a profressional car thief, there isn't really much you can do about it.  He will steal it.  And you will have no car. ||||reg||9
